; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Disk_PortA3_ClearAndSettle -- wait 10 ms, drive PA bit 3 LOW, wait 307 ms
; Called from: 3 calr site(s): 0xFE08C5, 0xFE09F1, 0xFE199D.  0xFE08C5 is 4
;          instructions into Disk_MountFloppyWithRetry and 0xFE199D is 2 into the routine at
;          0xFE1997 -- both at the head, before any disk request goes out.
;          0xFE09F1 is 20 instructions into DiskFormat_Execute and is preceded, by one
;          instruction, by a Disk_PortA3_Release call: that routine CYCLES the
;          line, release then assert.  Counts and distances from
;          `python3 notes/prom_a_pa3_census.py`.
; Inputs:  none.
; Outputs: PA bit 3 = 0.  BC clobbered by the two `popw bc`s.
; Evidence: `pushw 0x05 / calr Delay_Ticks / res 3,(0x1E) / calr Delay_150Ticks
;          / popw bc / ret`.  SFR 0x1E is PA (tmp95c061.cpp:1363, and
;          include/tmp95c061_sfr.inc).
; Unknown:  ⚠ what the pin is WIRED TO.  What IS established -- the writer
;          census, the 15 call sites, the assert-then-settle shape, and the
;          reset state -- is in notes/FINDINGS-prom_a-gap-T-pa3.md, re-derived
;          by `python3 notes/prom_a_pa3_census.py`.
;          ⚠ RENAMED 2026-08-25 (round-2 audit F5): this was
;          `Disk_PortA3_AssertAndSettle`.  "Assert" baked the active-low
;          READING into a permanent label; the name now states the DECODE
;          (bit 3 is cleared, then the routine waits).  That clearing is the
;          asserted direction -- only this direction is followed by a wait, and
;          RESET leaves the bit set -- remains the reading, and it lives here in
;          the header and in notes/FINDINGS-prom_a-gap-T-pa3.md, where it can be
;          contradicted.  What the pin is WIRED TO is still not established.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Disk_PortA3_ClearAndSettle:
	pushw 0x05                                           ; FE18E9  0b 05 00
	calr Delay_Ticks                                          ; FE18EC  1e 32 fb
	res	3, (PA:8)                                   ; FE18EF  f0 1e b3
	calr Delay_150Ticks                                          ; FE18F2  1e 1c fb
	popw bc                                              ; FE18F5  49
	ret                                                  ; FE18F6  0e
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Disk_PortA3_Release -- drive PA bit 3 HIGH, and flag the release
; Called from: 12 calr site(s): 0xFE0552, 0xFE0589, 0xFE095F, 0xFE09EE,
;          0xFE0A90, 0xFE11F1, 0xFE14C3, 0xFE15D5, 0xFE15E0, 0xFE15E5,
;          0xFE168B, 0xFE1CC4.
;          ELEVEN of the twelve are on an EXIT path: the linear stream from the
;          call reaches a `ret` within 12 instructions and issues no disk request
;          on the way (0 to 12 instructions; the last site 0xFE1CC4 is a bare
;          `calr .. / ret` veneer).  ⚠ The TWELFTH, 0xFE09EE, is not an exit --
;          the very next instruction, 0xFE09F1, calls
;          Disk_PortA3_ClearAndSettle, so DiskFormat_Execute CYCLES the line.  Measured
;          by `python3 notes/prom_a_pa3_census.py`, whose first draft asserted
;          "all twelve" and failed.
; Inputs:  (0x2076), a mode byte.
; Outputs: PA bit 3 = 1; and if (0x2076) != 0x0D then (0x2244) := 0xFF.
; Evidence: `set 3,(0x1E)`, then `cp (0x2076),0x0D / jr z / (0x2244) := 0xFF`.
;          There is NO delay here, and that asymmetry against
;          Disk_PortA3_ClearAndSettle is the reason LOW is read as the asserted
;          state.  RESET leaves the bit in THIS state: 0xF826D6 `ldio PA,0xF9`
;          with `PACR = 0x0E`, and PACR is the output enable
;          (tmp95c061.cpp:107 masks the driven value with it).
; Unknown:  what (0x2244) = 0xFF means to whoever reads it; what (0x2076) = 0x0D
;          selects.  And the same one as above: what the pin is wired to.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Disk_PortA3_Release:
	set	3, (PA:8)                                   ; FE18F7  f0 1e bb
	cp	(PanelModeGroup:16), 0x0d                            ; FE18FA  c1 76 20 3f 0d
	jr z, .LFE1906                                           ; FE18FF  66 05
	ld (0x2244:16), 0xff                                 ; FE1901  f1 44 22 00 ff
.LFE1906:
	ret                                                  ; FE1906  0e
