; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; DiskImage_HardDisk_MBR -- 512 bytes, a DOS master boot record
;
; Evidence: the standard layout, and a partition entry that agrees field for
; field with the boot sector above.
;
;   +0x000  x86 boot code: CLI / XOR AX,AX / MOV SS,AX / MOV SP,0x7C00 and the
;           0x0000:0x0600 relocation -- the textbook MBR preamble.  Strings
;           "Invalid partition table", "Error loading operating system",
;           "Missing operating system".
;   +0x1BE  partition entry 1:
;             boot flag  0x00   not bootable
;             start CHS  head 1, sector 1, cylinder 0
;             type       0x06   FAT16 over 32 MB
;             end CHS    head 14, sector 60, cylinder 567
;             LBA start  60         == the boot sector's hidden-sector count
;             sectors    511140     == the boot sector's total-sectors-32
;   +0x1CE  entries 2, 3 and 4: sixteen zero bytes each, i.e. unused
;   +0x1FE  55 AA
;
; ★ THE CROSS-CHECK: end CHS says cylinder 567, head 14, sector 60, i.e. the
;   last sector of a 568 x 15 x 60 disk counting cylinders and heads from 0 and
;   sectors from 1 -- the same geometry the BPB states, arrived at through a
;   different encoding (the two high cylinder bits live in the sector byte).
;
; Unknown:  the same one as the boot sector -- no consumer located.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
